## anthropics/claude-plugins-official

- Repository: https://github.com/anthropics/claude-plugins-official, commit `3b600518a637492d37c9877aeb49c2a55d939c04` (recorded in `upstream/sources.json`, read 2026-09-14; `plugins/code-modernization/` read 2026-09-19).
- License: Apache License 2.0. The repository ships the licence text at `LICENSE` and no `NOTICE` file, so there is no upstream notice to carry forward; the plugin declares its author as Anthropic (`plugins/frontend-design/.claude-plugin/plugin.json`).
- Adapted into `skills/bk-review/references/review-lenses.md` from `plugins/code-review/commands/code-review.md` and five agents of `plugins/pr-review-toolkit/` (code-reviewer, silent-failure-hunter, type-design-analyzer, code-simplifier, comment-analyzer): the review passes, the 0-100 confidence rubric and its anchors, the list of what is not a finding, and the per-lens checklists. The GitHub comment format and its link rules, the model-and-agent orchestration, the pull-request eligibility check and one project's own style rules are not carried.
- Adapted into `skills/bk-test/references/coverage-lens.md` from `plugins/pr-review-toolkit/agents/pr-test-analyzer.md`: behavioural coverage over line coverage, the gap list, the test-quality checks and the criticality scale.
- Adapted into `skills/bk-design/references/distinctive-ui.md` from `plugins/frontend-design/skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md`. The file is rewritten in the kit's form: the generic-default clusters, the typographic tells, the motion and hero rules, the two-pass process, the restraint rule and the writing rules are retained; the studio-persona framing and the client-relationship prose are not.
- The same text ships byte-identical in `anthropics/skills` at `skills/frontend-design/SKILL.md` (SHA-256 `b8009ae690dfa69edc7f08bb8715f32db8817112cfa4388741dbaf876c237df8`, checked 2026-09-11 and again 2026-09-14). This repository is named as the provenance because its release cycle is the clearer one, a decision recorded as question 14 of `docs/specs/2026-09-12-d5-owner-questions.md`.
- Adapted into `skills/bk-map/references/codebase-map.md` from `plugins/code-modernization/agents/legacy-analyst.md` and `plugins/code-modernization/commands/modernize-map.md`, into `skills/bk-map/references/first-contact.md` from `plugins/code-modernization/commands/modernize-preflight.md`, and into `skills/bk-map/references/business-rules.md` from `plugins/code-modernization/agents/business-rules-extractor.md` and `plugins/code-modernization/commands/modernize-extract-rules.md`: the reading discipline, the rules that keep a dependency map honest, the owner questions asked without blocking, the build definition as ground truth, the scope boundary, and the business-rule card with its priority heuristic. The plugin ships its own `LICENSE`, byte-identical to the Apache License 2.0 at the repository root, and no `NOTICE`. The mainframe vocabulary, the extraction script and its interactive viewer, and the workflow orchestration are not carried.
- Nothing is vendored from `claude-code-setup` in the same repository, and on present evidence nothing will be: it was read in full on 2026-09-15 and inventoried at zero items absorbed, because it recommends host-specific automation and MCP servers the kit does not install. The reasoning is in `docs/specs/2026-09-11-skill-inventory.md`; whether the source stays ideas-only is the owner's call.

